{"id":"959f67178eec388a","group":"93","path":"93/93-df-consistency.md","title":"Consistency","display":"df-consistency — Consistency","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-df-consistency","aliases":["93-df-consistency"],"display":"df-consistency — Consistency","depends_on":["[[93-df-logic]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-df-consistency"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-df-consistency</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-consistency — Consistency"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"bd7e4207897c8db3\" href=\"?note=bd7e4207897c8db3\" title=\"93-df-logic\">93-df-logic</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf L\">\\(\\mathsf L\\)</span> is a candidate ordered pair consisting of a formula set and a consequence relation.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Logic}\">\\(\\mathrm{Logic}\\)</span> is the sourced finitary structural-logic predicate.</li>\n<li>Consistency is taken in the intrinsic nontriviality sense: not every formula follows from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}\\)</span> is the consistency predicate defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}consistency}\\vdash\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(T,\\mathsf L)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\;\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\mathsf L=\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Logic}(F,\\vdash_{\\mathsf L})\\\\\n&amp;\\land T\\subseteq F\n\\land\\exists\\varphi\\in F\\;\\neg(T\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\varphi)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}consistency}\\vdash\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(T,\\mathsf L)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\;\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\mathsf L=\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Logic}(F,\\vdash_{\\mathsf L})\\\\\n&amp;\\land T\\subseteq F\n\\land\\exists\\varphi\\in F\\;\\neg(T\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\varphi)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The formula universe and consequence relation are bound by the displayed logic object. For an explosive logic with a contradiction constant, this intrinsic nontriviality condition is equivalent to failure to derive that constant.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-logic","status":"resolved","id":"bd7e4207897c8db3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-logic]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathsf L","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Logic}","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}consistency}\\vdash\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(T,\\mathsf L)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists F\\;\\exists\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\;\\Bigl[{}&\n\\mathsf L=\\langle F,\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Logic}(F,\\vdash_{\\mathsf L})\\\\\n&\\land T\\subseteq F\n\\land\\exists\\varphi\\in F\\;\\neg(T\\vdash_{\\mathsf L}\\varphi)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":1193,"backlinks":[{"id":"dc3498f98607795c","anchor":"ref-11","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}$, $\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}$, and $\\mathrm{CompleteTh}_{93}$ are the predicates of [[93-df-maximal-theory]], [[93-df-consistency]], and [[93-df-complete-theory]]."},{"id":"def48430496c026c","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"8bbd77b21a9519f1","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}$ is the nontriviality predicate of [[93-df-consistency]], and $\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}$ is defined here."},{"id":"882ddfff5f1c7a82","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"ea98968ac191af8c","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["bd7e4207897c8db3"]}